  <entry>
    <id>https://doi.org/10.1287/mksc.2025.0145</id>
    <title>Visual Plant Imagery and Property Valuation: A Descriptive Analysis</title>
    <updated>2026-10-05T00:00:00+00:00</updated>
    <author>
      <name>Yuqian Chang, Nathan Fong, Ning Ye, Maureen (Mimi) Morrin</name>
    </author>
    <content>&lt;b&gt;Marketing Science&lt;/b&gt; &lt;br&gt;Online home profiles with more plant imagery are associated with higher property valuations, even after accounting for extensive property, neighborhood, listing, and market factors.</content>
    <link href="https://doi.org/10.1287/mksc.2025.0145"/>
